                <pb facs="0395" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg281"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Turkish Diplomatic Mission to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>During the present session of the Council of the League of Nations, Lord Balfour
                    asked that the Palestine Mandate be assigned to England.</p>
                <p>The Turkish Diplomatic Mission, esteeming that no part of the territory of the
                    Ottoman Empire can be legally decided upon before a definitive peace has been
                    concluded with Turkey, protests in the name of its Government against all
                    eventual decisions on this matter and considers as null and void the decisions
                    taken without its consent.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
